  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=2{X}^{3}+1.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $b$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $c$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=2{X}^{3}+1$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,$ $b=1,$ $c=0.4,$ and $a+b+c=0.4.$",
